            <div xml:id="d171">

                <pb facs="0419" n="335" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg335"/>

                <head>No. 167.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Phelps.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-05-21"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 21,
                        1886</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 303.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my instruction No. 289 of
                    the 11th instant, transmitting to you a copy of my note of the 10th of this
                    month to Sir Lionel West, Her Britannic Majesty’s minister at this capital,
                    concerning the fishery question, I now inclose for your information a copy of a
                    further note on the same subject, which I addressed to Sir Lionel West
                    yesterday, inclosing also a copy of the report of the United States
                    consul-general at Halifax, which is referred to in my note to Sir Lionel
                    West.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>T. F. BAYARD.</signed></closer>











